<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ilkhan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ilkhan was the title adopted by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hulagu-khan">Hulagu</a> and his successors, meaning a subordinate khan. It acknowledged the nominal supremacy of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-khan">Great Khan</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a>. The title gave its name to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a>, the Mongol state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>.</p></div>
